Today we're gonna try and make this super cool looking

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:21.390
cotton candy called dragon beard's candy.

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:23.410
This candy originated from China,

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:26.220
apparently ancient emperor's used to eat this.

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:29.513
Think of cotton candy that's made purely from your hands.

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:31.240
That's pretty cool.

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:34.008
Success rate is super, super low,

00:00:34.008 --> 00:00:35.660
but we're still gonna give it a shot.

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:36.493
Let's do it.

00:00:36.493 --> 00:00:38.320
The ingredients are pretty simple.

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:40.940
It's basically just sugar, sugar, sugar, sugar, and water.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:44.390
Sugar, water, corn syrup, vinegar, maltose.

00:00:44.390 --> 00:00:46.899
You put them all in this pot, boil them up until

00:00:46.899 --> 00:00:49.490
it becomes this sticky, gooey liquid

00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:52.750
that we're then gonna shape into candy.

00:00:52.750 --> 00:00:56.440
I also got burn relief gel because I wasn't sure

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:58.070
if I would burn myself.

00:00:58.070 --> 00:00:59.300
So one step at a time.

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:01.570
If I remember correctly what I was supposed to do.

00:01:01.570 --> 00:01:02.963
So sugar first.

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:06.937
Ooh hoo hoo.

00:01:07.110 --> 00:01:09.763
Get every single bit.

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:10.913
Maltose.

00:01:10.913 --> 00:01:12.060
Super gooey.

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:13.360
That's what it looks like.

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:17.100
From the videos and the recipes I saw,

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:19.390
I'm supposed to turn this on and then not stir it.

00:01:19.390 --> 00:01:22.010
If you stir it, the sugar's gonna crystallize,

00:01:22.010 --> 00:01:25.010
and if it crystallizes, you're screwed.

00:01:25.010 --> 00:01:26.390
And that is a big no-no.

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:27.223
Oh my god.

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:31.100
Okay, so now I'm supposed to just leave it running.

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:33.550
I'm not the most patient person in the world, so.

00:01:33.852 --> 00:01:36.352
(light music)

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:45.640
^It's about 225, looks like a little volcano.

